+# M8-01 discovery implementation — 2026-10-06
+
+Status: **DONE_WITH_CONCERNS**, subject to coordinator review. M8-01's isolated discovery behavior is implemented; no module, physical-controller, deployment, endpoint or platform compatibility gate is credited here. Shared checkboxes and progress were left to the coordinator.
+
+Review base: `4082deb639d4aca5451d9df2580d06c74e6bb34a`, branch `ftc-workspace`. Checks executed on that revision plus the scoped working-tree changes described below. The implementation revision is the focused `feat(ftc): parse discovery and authorization states` commit containing this report and its logs; the coordinator records its resulting hash after creation. To identify exactly what was tested without a self-referential commit hash, these are the final Git blob revisions:
+
+| File                                                          | Tested blob                                |
+| ------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
+| `packages/schema/src/ftc-controller.ts`                       | `55d3c1e8b4ff179868934740ccbc9adad71b984c` |
+| `packages/schema/src/index.ts`                                | `840451bcc36c2d6bee478fbb3dd5cc2c04baf94a` |
+| `packages/core/src/ftc/controllers.ts`                        | `9cb602d6433cd1cea8a5968bcf404b9c95b570d4` |
+| `packages/core/src/ftc/controllers/adb.ts`                    | `14012efff11aced5b8584fef831dcb6a592a247e` |
+| `packages/core/test/ftc/controller-connections/m8-01.test.ts` | `f0c9fbdb531ae3a15bb6154803e100416bdc7d51` |
+
+Environment: macOS 26.5.2, build 25F84, arm64; Bun **1.3.14** (`0d9b296a`); repository Effect **4.0.0-beta.83**. OS/architecture verified using `sw_vers` and `uname -m`; Bun verified with `/private/tmp/ftc-bun-1.3.14/bun-darwin-aarch64/bun --version`, all exit 0. Dependencies were already provisioned; no dependency/tool installation or manifest/lockfile changes were made. Windows execution was not available and was not run.
+
+## Implementation and decisions
+
+- Schema owns the sole `FtcController.ControllerCandidate` and structured `DiscoveryError`. Public records are readonly Schema values with stable domain identifiers. The canonical current contract is exported from the existing Schema barrel as required by its package guide. Core re-exports those exact schema identities.
+- `Controllers.Service` is an Effect facade built by `Controllers.layer(transport)`. Its narrow injected `Adb.DiscoveryTransport.readDevices` accepts only the structured argument tuple `["devices", "-l"]`; it has no install/start/connect/forward/shell or mutation operation. No host binding, daemon, global coordinator, application registry or sibling bootstrap was added.
+- Pure `Adb.parseDevices` parses `devices -l` responses. It retains transport address, reported ADB state and optional reported model. Authorization and availability are distinct: `device` yields authorized/available; `unauthorized` yields unauthorized/unauthorized; `offline` yields unknown/offline. Unrecognized states, including the multi-word ADB permission diagnostic, remain unknown/unavailable with `adb_unsupported_state`.
+- Ruling agreed with the coordinator: a successful header with no devices yields `[]`; absent/malformed output is `adb_invalid_response`. Missing tools, transport failures and nonzero command exits are typed failures (`adb_missing_tool`, `adb_transport_error`, `adb_command_failed`) rather than fabricated candidates or empty-success results. Invalid rows, invalid metadata, duplicate metadata keys and repeated transport addresses fail the whole response conservatively.
+- Exact reported `model:REV_Control_Hub` produces an optional `control-hub` kind hint. Generic Android models remain of unknown kind, including the phone-shaped synthetic fixture. ADB authorization/availability and model hints establish neither FTC compatibility nor stable physical identity. No `controllerID`, alias mapping, target selection, generation or connection descriptor was introduced; those remain later owners' work.
+- Language-independent guidance codes cover Control Hub connections, identifying Control Hub/phone hardware, unverified phone compatibility, USB authorization, connection recovery and unobserved Expansion Hub configuration. They are setup/recovery context, not observations of attached Expansion Hubs, wiring or robot configuration. No UI copy or untranslated presentation text was added.
+- Import/layer construction does not run discovery. Each call owns an `Effect.scoped` read, preserving interruption and closing the injected transport's per-read finalizers on success, parse failure, command failure, transport failure and cancellation. The external host owns its transport; this task owns no process, polling subscription, forward or persistent/global map to dispose.
+
+## Task assertions and gates
+
+| Required assertion/gate                             | Concrete evidence                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
+| --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Focused unauthorized-device test                    | `unauthorized device is visible without deployment side effects` exercises the real service and parser. It asserts `candidate.authorization === "unauthorized"`, address/state/error code, exactly one discovery tuple and `mutationCalls === []`. The fixture records any non-discovery invocation as a mutation violation.                                                                                                                                                |
+| Behavioral RED before discovery implementation      | Tests were written first. Minimal Schema/port/service scaffolding returned `[]` to permit real facade imports without a broken harness. [RED](m8-01/red.log.gz): exit 1, 0 pass / 18 fail / 11 assertions. The named test failed on expected length 1 versus actual length 0. Cancellation also timed out because the stub never entered the read port; there were no import/module-resolution failures. The parser and transport read execution were added only afterward. |
+| Available/offline/unauthorized and multiple devices | Multiple-target CRLF fixture asserts exact authorization/state/address triples, reported models and offline cause; the unauthorized test covers the other branch. No target is automatically selected.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
