+| Successful empty versus missing-tool/error          | Empty-header fixture returns `[]`; missing output and malformed records fail. Command exit, missing-tool and transport-error tests preserve separate codes and structured details.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
+| Control Hub/phone and Expansion Hub context         | Multiple-target fixture asserts known Control Hub hint, unknown generic Android kind, phone compatibility/identification guidance and Expansion Hub configuration-unobserved guidance. It asserts absence of identity/aliases, attached-hub and wiring claims.                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
+| Canonical serializable readonly contract            | Runtime test asserts exact facade/Schema identity, decodes real output, verifies omitted optional fields during encoding, rejects guessed authorization and empty addresses, and round-trips JSON. Schema/Core typechecks pass.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
+| No discovery or mutation at construction            | Four cleanup cases provide the real layer without invoking discovery and assert zero read acquisitions; named unauthorized test asserts the only issued command tuple and no mutation violation. Source has no process/network/ADB binding or import-time I/O.                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
+| Cleanup and cancellation                            | Four cleanup cases observe zero active read resources after success/malformed/command/transport results. Cancellation test interrupts the in-flight read and observes failure plus zero remaining resources. Two fresh scopes return fresh results and acquire three distinct resources overall, including the cancelled read.                                                                                                                                              |
+| GREEN and scoped review                             | [Final focused log](m8-01/green-final.log): exit 0, 22 pass / 0 fail / 81 assertions. Source diff was reviewed against the declared base, scoped lint/format and `git diff --check` pass. Only assigned files, required Schema barrel and owned report/logs are staged.                                                                                                                                                                                                     |
