+## Fixture versus real limits and cleanup
+
+All discovery transcripts and error responses are synthetic, inline `adb devices -l` format fixtures with addresses `SERIAL_A`, `USB_A`, `PHONE_A`, `192.0.2.3:5555` and `FRESH`. They exercise the actual Effect facade and pure parser, not a substitute discovery algorithm. These results validate fixture parsing and lifecycle behavior on the available macOS host only. No ADB binary was executed, daemon started, controller contacted, robot mutated, forwarding created or user application/service restarted. No physical attachment, wiring, supported phone matrix, USB/Wi-Fi reachability, stable identity, Panels endpoint or actual deployment was established. Those need M8-02/M8-04/M8-06 and M9 evidence.
+
+The isolated suite creates only test-owned in-memory resource tokens; each lifecycle assertion observes zero active tokens after completion/interruption. No ADB/controller transport process, port listener, scratch tool installation or temporary resource directory was created by this task. Raw RED and full Schema output are gzip-compressed to retain the complete baseline comparison without a large raw AST diff. Only the five product/test paths and this report/log directory belong to the commit; pre-existing and concurrent coordinator documents remain unstaged and unchanged by this worker. No checklist or ledger was edited, no reviewer/subagent dispatched, and no generated client/SDK regeneration is required because Protocol/HttpApi/legacy SDK surfaces were untouched.
